FLOWDATA=[
('instruction-confirmation','Instruction and confirmation','Instruct settlement, booking or movement of securities and report processing and settlement.','External process such as exchange/OTC trade, realignment, repo trade or portfolio transfer.','The high-level Instruction definition states None.','Acknowledgement of acceptance at the Instruction-process boundary. The full exchange ends with settlement confirmation.',[17,28],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.023.001.13','sese.024.001.14','sese.025.001.13'],'§4 Instruction table17; §5.1 table28; §6.1 paragraphs324–327','The instructing party sends sese.023. The executing/servicing party may return processing and/or settlement status using sese.024. When settlement takes place it sends sese.025. Successful validation can also lead to a status update even though that path is omitted from the activity diagram.','01-typical-sequence'),
('partial-settlement','Partial settlement confirmation','Report a single instruction settling in multiple phases while retaining the original instruction.','Transaction settles only in part.','No separate formal precondition list is provided in §6.3; its exchange starts with an instruction.','Confirmation of the remaining quantity completes the exchange described in §6.3.',[],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.023.001.13','sese.024.001.14','sese.025.001.13'],'§6.3 paragraphs336–342','Instructing party sends sese.023; optional processing/settlement statuses use sese.024. Servicer confirms only the partially settled quantity with sese.025, may report the still-pending quantity’s status, then confirms the remaining quantity when settled. This is not instruction splitting: the original instruction is retained.','02-partial-sequence'),
('cancellation-request','Cancellation request','Request cancellation of an open transaction.','Need to cancel an open transaction, or first modification step where transaction data cannot be amended.','An open transaction exists and cancellation is possible.','Acknowledgement of cancellation-request processing; the completed exchange returns cancellation-request status completed.',[19,45],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.023.001.13','sese.020.001.09','sese.027.001.09'],'§4 Cancellation Request table19; §5.12 table45; §6.12 paragraphs607–612','After original instruction, instructing party sends sese.020. Executing/servicing party validates and attempts cancellation. It may return intermediate status and returns completion using sese.027. Request submission does not itself establish cancellation. Source permits successful-validation status updates intentionally omitted from its activity diagram.','03-cancellation-sequence'),
('cancellation-advice','Cancellation advice','Advise cancellation of an earlier communication sent by executing/servicing party.','Previous communication is identified as inaccurate or void.','A previous communication has taken place.','High-level process definition states None.',[25,46],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['semt.020.001.07'],'§4 Cancellation Advice table25; §5.13 table46 and paragraphs306–308; §6.13 paragraphs615–620','Executing/servicing party sends advice, statement or confirmation, then semt.020 to cancel that communication, for example if sent in error. Status of a cancellation request belongs to cancellation-request reporting. Source conflict: §5.13 paragraph308 routes instructions cancelled by servicer/third party to instruction-status reporting; §6.13 paragraph619 points to reversal advice. Preserve both claims; do not make an unqualified routing rule.','04-cancellation-advice-sequence'),
('reversal-advice','Settlement reversal advice','Reverse a confirmed transaction and return it to open status.','Transaction should not have been confirmed, or receiving party returned shares.','Transaction has been confirmed and reversal is possible.','Underlying instruction remains in settlement processing; account owner receives statuses and confirmations.',[22,47],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.025.001.13','sese.026.001.12'],'§4 Reversal table22; §5.14 table47; §6.14 paragraphs624–625','After settlement confirmation, executing party sends sese.026 to instructing party to reverse confirmation of partial/full delivery or receipt, free/against payment, physically/by book-entry. This differs from an account owner requesting cancellation of an open transaction.','05-reversal-sequence'),
('reporting-push','Reconciliation and reporting: push mode','Provide data for reconciliation of holdings, transactions and allegements.','Account setup and account-owner reporting requirements.','High-level Reconciliation definition states None.','High-level definition states None; detected breaks may lead to investigation and other processes.',[26,43],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party','reporting-third-party'],['semt.002.001.12','semt.003.001.12','semt.016.001.10','semt.017.001.14','semt.018.001.15','semt.019.001.12','semt.022.001.07'],'§4 Reconciliation table26; §5.11 Push Mode paragraphs275–286 and table43','Executing/servicing party provides statements according to setup and SLA; not all reports are always supplied. Instructing party reconciles holdings and transactions, then investigates breaks. A third party may receive audit trail for each individual pending instruction covering its status and modification history. Keep this participant even if a two-party diagram omits it.',None),
('reporting-pull','Reconciliation and reporting: pull mode','Respond to a request for statement or transaction status.','Receipt of statement/status request.','No additional formal pull-mode precondition list is provided.','Requested statement/status is returned after successful processing; request status may also be advised.',[44],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party','reporting-third-party'],['semt.021.001.09','sese.021.001.08','sese.022.001.08','semt.022.001.07'],'§5.11 Pull Mode paragraphs288–300 and table44; §6.11 paragraphs602–604','Instructing party sends SecuritiesStatementQuery or SecuritiesTransactionStatusQuery. Executing party validates request and may return SecuritiesStatusOrStatementQueryStatusAdvice before requested report. A third party can request a detailed report on a pending transaction and receive audit trail. Statement selection, optional request status and failed validation are separate decisions.',None),
('portfolio-transfer','Portfolio transfer','Exchange settlement details for full or partial client portfolio transfer.','Client intends to move some or all positions to another custodian.','No formal precondition list is stated in §5.15/§6.15.','After reconciliation without breaks, receiving custodian instructs receives-free and delivering custodian instructs deliveries-free to CSD.',[48],['portfolio-transfer-client','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.037.001.09','sese.023.001.13'],'§5.15 table48; §6.15 paragraphs628–630','Client advises both custodians. Custodians process request, exchange details and reconcile them. Breaks lead to client investigation and potentially an updated move. Sequence highlights only two servicing parties; narrative/table also include client and instructions to CSD. Delivering custodian may include a receiving settlement chain for validation; if unavailable, receiving custodian can return it in same message type.',None),
('transaction-generation','Transaction generation notification','Advise an instructing party that a servicing party generated a settlement transaction for it.','Examples: automatic transformation of pending instructions after a corporate event, or account-owner transaction-database recovery initiated by servicing party.','No formal precondition list is provided.','Instructing party is informed of generated transaction.',[],['instructing-party','executing-servicing-party'],['sese.032.001.13'],'§5.16 paragraphs314–315; §6.16 paragraphs633–634','Executing/servicing party sends SecuritiesSettlementTransactionGenerationNotification to instructing party. Cited paragraphs do not prescribe a response, failure branch or further activity sequence.',None)]
